{
  "description": "Story 20.4 — calculation cases of invoice collections (acompte, paiements partiels, échéancier, retard): exactly what the API serves, computed by the backend through the same code path (PaymentStateCalculator.afterChange then view; test PaymentStateCalculatorTest), reusable by the Bref React Native app. Amounts in XAF francs (integers). Rows: a payment received has paidAt (yyyy-MM-dd); a scheduled instalment has dueDate (and paidAt once settled). amountDue = totalTtc − creditedTtc; amountPaid = sum of rows with paidAt. cases: storedState = the state stored before the change (null: never computed); newRow = the row added by the change (refused with OVERPAYMENT when the sum of all rows would exceed amountDue — remaining = amountDue − sum of existing rows —, with VALIDATION_ERROR when an instalment's dueDate is before today); expected.state = the state served after the change: PAID if amountPaid >= amountDue; otherwise OVERDUE only if storedState was already OVERDUE and an unpaid row is still past due (dueDate < today, Africa/Douala); otherwise PARTIAL if amountPaid > 0, else UNPAID — a change never makes an invoice overdue. A case without newRow and with storedState null is a read of an invoice whose state was never stored (legacy: issued without row → UNPAID). action cancel: an issued invoice with at least one payment received cannot be cancelled (INVOICE_INVALID_TRANSITION). jobCases: the daily overdue job (07:00 Africa/Douala) on an active ISSUED invoice: marked (→ OVERDUE, owner notified once per run) when an unpaid row is past due and the stored state is neither OVERDUE nor PAID.",
